# Tilemaps and collision
@scenario tutorial_lesson_43
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/43_tilemap_world.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt open_world]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: The workshop map uses two tiles: floor and brick. Move the green marker with the arrow keys and try crossing the brick wall.
@label lab
> Walk the map -> demo
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
@label demo
# region open_world
[jes push scripts/scenes/tile_world.jes label compare]
# endregion
@label compare
[set tutorial_source scripts/scenes/tile_world.jes]
[set tutorial_excerpt map]
ginger: Change a brick tile from 1 to -1 in assets/tutorial/labs/walls.csv. Reopen the map and walk through the gap. The collision layer consumes the same data as the image layer.
[jump lab]
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_43]
[flag tutorial_done_43]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_9]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Replace one brick with -1. What changes?
> The entire map shrinks. -> practice_hint
> That brick and its collider disappear. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: A collision-enabled layer interprets nonempty tiles as blocked cells.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: A collision-enabled layer interprets nonempty tiles as blocked cells.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Which CSV layer determines whether a tile blocks movement?
> The collision layer. -> correct
> The floor layer with collision disabled. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
ginger: A collision-enabled layer interprets nonempty tiles as blocked cells.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: A collision-enabled layer interprets nonempty tiles as blocked cells.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
